WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:29.875


2
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:33.791
<b>After naming the exceptionally </b>
<b>skilled warriors of his army</b>

3
00:00:33.791 --> 00:00:37.875
<b>Duryodhana now encourages the</b>
<b>rest of the soldiers. </b>

4
00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:38.750
<b>He says, </b>

5
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.708
<b>"All of you warriors,</b>

6
00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:43.625
<b>stand firm in your assigned positions </b>

7
00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:46.458
<b>and protect Grandsire Bhishma."</b>

8
00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:51.291


9
00:00:51.291 --> 00:00:52.666
<b>Say what you will,</b>

10
00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:54.916
<b>Duryodhana is indeed shrewd. </b>

11
00:00:54.916 --> 00:00:56.041
<b>Here</b>

12
00:00:56.041 --> 00:00:57.625
<b>Just a moment ago, </b>

13
00:00:57.625 --> 00:01:01.500
<b>he named all the warriors in his army</b>

14
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.166
<b>whom he wanted to win over by</b>
<b>making them feel special. </b>

15
00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:09.416
<b>Now, addressing the rest,</b>

16
00:01:09.416 --> 00:01:11.583
<b>he calls them warriors, </b>

17
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:16.166
<b>making them aware of the importance of</b>
<b>their position in the army. </b>

18
00:01:16.166 --> 00:01:19.541
<b>Grandsire Bhishma is the greatest warrior, </b>

19
00:01:19.541 --> 00:01:22.458
<b>the commander-in-chief of the Kaurava army. </b>

20
00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:23.166
<b>But</b>

21
00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:25.166
<b>more importantly, </b>

22
00:01:25.166 --> 00:01:28.375
<b>he has been granted the boon of choosing</b>
<b>the time of his own death. </b>

23
00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:31.375
<b>He will not die without his wish.</b>

24
00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:32.250
<b>In such a case,</b>

25
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:38.333
<b>having Grandsire Bhishma with</b>
<b>any army can make that army invincible. </b>

26
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:40.333
<b>And protecting such a warrior </b>

27
00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.708
<b>increases the chances of victory </b>

28
00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:45.916
<b>and is also a matter of great pride. </b>

29
00:01:45.916 --> 00:01:47.208
<b>He is saying</b>

30
00:01:47.208 --> 00:01:49.125
<b>that you are all warriors, </b>

31
00:01:49.125 --> 00:01:54.416
<b>and your position in this war</b>
<b>is of utmost importance.</b>

32
00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:59.208


33
00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:03.375
<b>We find examples, not once but many times, </b>

34
00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:04.750
<b>that Duryodhana</b>

35
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.458
<b>is not only cunning </b>

36
00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:10.083
<b>but also an excellent diplomat.</b>

37
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:12.833
<b>He knows well </b>

38
00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:17.000
<b>when to make someone feel important, </b>

39
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.541
<b>whose sore spot to touch, </b>

40
00:02:20.541 --> 00:02:24.333
<b>how to inspire everyone </b>

41
00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:30.000
<b>that if you just keep at it, victory will be ours. </b>

42
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.833
<b>Whatever doubts there may be in the mind, </b>

43
00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:36.666
<b>he chooses his heavy words carefully. </b>

44
00:02:36.666 --> 00:02:41.250
<b>He is indeed a highly effective speaker. </b>

45
00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:44.500
<b>But his purpose is corrupt, </b>

46
00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.791
<b>and his mind is tainted with unrighteousness. </b>

47
00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:50.000
<b>And so this, </b>

48
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.916
<b>This itself will lead towards defeat and death, </b>

49
00:02:52.916 --> 00:02:55.208
<b>not only him </b>

50
00:02:55.208 --> 00:03:02.625
<b>but every person who supports him </b>

51
00:03:02.625 --> 00:03:06.291
<b>The perfume bottle we buy</b>

52
00:03:06.291 --> 00:03:08.541
<b>is very alluring,</b>

53
00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:10.291
<b>isn’t it? </b>

54
00:03:10.291 --> 00:03:15.875
<b>the outer fragrance of</b>
<b>the perfume is also intoxicating, </b>

55
00:03:15.875 --> 00:03:20.833
<b>but if you consume the perfume kept inside, </b>

56
00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.916
<b>if you drink it, </b>

57
00:03:23.916 --> 00:03:28.416
<b>it acts as poison.</b>

58
00:03:28.416 --> 00:03:30.375
<b>On the other hand, </b>

59
00:03:30.375 --> 00:03:32.458
<b>an earthen pot </b>

60
00:03:32.458 --> 00:03:34.750
<b>may look ungainly, </b>

61
00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:39.083
<b>the water kept in it may have no fragrance, </b>

62
00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:40.875
<b>but it is </b>

63
00:03:40.875 --> 00:03:45.583
<b> life-giving. </b>

64
00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:47.333
<b>What is inside</b>

65
00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:49.666
<b>is more important. </b>

66
00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:50.916
<b>without knowing, </b>

67
00:03:50.916 --> 00:03:59.916
<b>being attracted only by the outward appearance,</b>

68
00:03:59.916 --> 00:04:01.208
<b>We too</b>

69
00:04:01.208 --> 00:04:03.708
<b>get inspired by a person's outer shine, </b>

70
00:04:03.708 --> 00:04:05.958
<b>by seeing their way of speaking,</b>

71
00:04:05.958 --> 00:04:07.916
<b>by listening to their lofty words. </b>

72
00:04:07.916 --> 00:04:10.875
<b>get inspired by it.</b>

73
00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:13.958
<b>We wish to be like them. </b>

74
00:04:13.958 --> 00:04:17.333
<b>We even side with them. </b>

75
00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:19.125
<b>But if </b>

76
00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.541
<b>their character is corrupt,</b>

77
00:04:21.541 --> 00:04:23.916
<b>if their purpose is impure, </b>

78
00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:28.875
<b>then supporting them is detrimental. </b>

79
00:04:28.875 --> 00:04:30.791
<b>Before we realize it, </b>

80
00:04:30.791 --> 00:04:31.625
<b>we too</b>

81
00:04:31.625 --> 00:04:34.083
<b> will have gone down the wrong path, </b>

82
00:04:34.083 --> 00:04:37.708
<b>our minds will also start getting tainted.</b>

83
00:04:37.708 --> 00:04:41.375
<b>Be careful.</b>

84
00:04:41.375 --> 00:04:43.416
<b>Now you will say, </b>

85
00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:47.833
<b>how can one discern what's in someone's mind?</b>

86
00:04:47.833 --> 00:04:49.666
<b>Have patience. </b>

87
00:04:49.666 --> 00:04:53.041
<b>This Gita has the answer to that as well. </b>

88
00:04:53.041 --> 00:04:55.375
<b>There is an answer to your every question, </b>

89
00:04:55.375 --> 00:04:59.250
<b>and all those answers will come at the right time.</b>

90
00:04:59.708 --> 00:05:03.916


91
00:05:03.916 --> 00:05:06.083
<b>In an earlier section, </b>

92
00:05:06.083 --> 00:05:08.333
<b>we learned </b>

93
00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:09.458
<b>that how</b>

94
00:05:09.458 --> 00:05:12.625
<b>Dhritarashtra's royal greed and his son </b>

95
00:05:12.625 --> 00:05:15.750
<b>Shakuni's conspiracies led his nephew </b>

96
00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:20.083
<b>Duryodhana astray.</b>

97
00:05:20.083 --> 00:05:21.625
<b>but </b>

98
00:05:21.625 --> 00:05:25.708
<b>now let's talk about some gentlemen</b>

99
00:05:25.708 --> 00:05:30.208
<b>How did Duryodhana's morale</b>
<b>increase for this war? </b>

100
00:05:30.208 --> 00:05:36.125
<b>How did he come to believe that even if</b>
<b>he stands with unrighteousness, </b>

101
00:05:36.125 --> 00:05:37.541
<b>there are some people </b>

102
00:05:37.541 --> 00:05:39.500
<b>who will not stop him, </b>

103
00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.708
<b>who will stand by him?</b>

104
00:05:43.708 --> 00:05:45.291
<b>Grandsire Bhishma</b>

105
00:05:45.291 --> 00:05:47.500
<b>and Guru Drona, </b>

106
00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:50.208
<b>they are indeed gentlemen.</b>

107
00:05:50.208 --> 00:05:53.833
<b>But when Draupadi's disrobing was happening</b>
<b>in the grand assembly, </b>

108
00:05:53.833 --> 00:05:56.041
<b>these two remained silent. </b>

109
00:05:56.041 --> 00:05:58.125
<b>Even if unspoken, </b>

110
00:05:58.125 --> 00:06:04.583
<b>their silence contributes to</b>
<b>Duryodhana's encouragement.</b>

111
00:06:04.583 --> 00:06:08.750
<b>Being a gentleman does not mean staying quiet. </b>

112
00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.166
<b>It is the responsibility of the elders of the house </b>

113
00:06:11.166 --> 00:06:13.625
<b>that if there is ever a violation of etiquette, </b>

114
00:06:13.625 --> 00:06:16.000
<b>it should be stopped right then and there. </b>

115
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.500
<b>And if this is not done,</b>

116
00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:22.958
<b>then rude behavior will become a habit</b>

117
00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:27.625


118
00:06:27.625 --> 00:06:29.708
<b>How wonderful it would have been </b>

119
00:06:29.708 --> 00:06:31.041
<b>if </b>

120
00:06:31.041 --> 00:06:34.791
<b> Duryodhana's purpose was also pure.</b>

121
00:06:34.791 --> 00:06:35.708
<b>Because</b>

122
00:06:35.708 --> 00:06:37.625
<b>he is indeed a successful diplomat, </b>

123
00:06:37.625 --> 00:06:41.125
<b>an influential speaker. </b>

124
00:06:41.125 --> 00:06:44.291
<b>There is much to learn from him too.</b>

125
00:06:44.291 --> 00:06:45.458
<b>Here,</b>

126
00:06:45.458 --> 00:06:49.791
<b>while assigning tasks to everyone,</b>
<b>he tells them how </b>

127
00:06:49.791 --> 00:06:53.250
<b>great their contribution is</b>

128
00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:56.416
<b> if they have kept the great Bhishma safe,</b>

129
00:06:56.416 --> 00:07:00.250
<b>then the greatest victory will also be theirs.</b>

130
00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.500
<b>When a member of your organization, </b>

131
00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:06.041
<b>every person in your organization, </b>

132
00:07:06.041 --> 00:07:10.333
<b>starts considering himself</b>
<b>a participant in a big goal, </b>

133
00:07:10.333 --> 00:07:14.041
<b>then his energy automatically increases. </b>

134
00:07:14.041 --> 00:07:16.291
<b>His work starts looking big to him. </b>

135
00:07:16.291 --> 00:07:18.291
<b>The goal becomes supreme. </b>

136
00:07:18.291 --> 00:07:22.875
<b>They now see their victory in your victory.</b>

137
00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:26.416
<b>Explain the importance of everyone's work, </b>

138
00:07:26.416 --> 00:07:30.750
<b>keep making them aware of this importance.</b>

139
00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:35.958
<b>And don't miss publicly praising good work.</b>

